    "TER": "Semicap automated test equipment geared to AI chip test volume | strengthening",
    "TSM": "Foundry monopoly manufacturing leading-edge AI chips | strengthening",
    "MU": "Memory (DRAM/HBM). THESIS THREAT 2026-07-28: CXMT listed on Shanghai STAR (+400% debut) -- China's domestic DRAM champion is now publicly capitalised, on top of HBM3E ASP -51% from peak. Named, funded competitor where there was none | watch",
    "SNDK": "AI NAND/enterprise-SSD supercycle. Same CXMT capitalisation threat as MU; highest beta in book (2.464) and 1.6x its risk cap | watch",
    "AMAT": "Semicap deposition/etch equipment for AI chip fabs (position cut to dust, 0.012% weight -- sizing only, thesis unaffected) | strengthening",
    "COHR": "Photonics/optical components for datacenter interconnect | strengthening",
    "ARM": "Chip architecture/IP licensing powering most AI silicon | watch",
    "AMD": "GPU/CPU compute silicon, direct AI-accelerator competitor to NVDA | strengthening",
    "ORCL": "Oracle Cloud Infrastructure -- hyperscaler cloud/AI-capex beneficiary | watch",
    "GOOG": "Hyperscaler that BUYS AI capex rather than selling it -- the chain's only internal hedge; blowout 2Q26 print, no earnings until ~late Oct | strengthening [POSITION CLOSED 2026-07-28, swapped to GOOGL Class A]",
    "GOOGL": "Alphabet Class A \u2014 replaced the Class C holding 2026-07-28. Hyperscaler that BUYS AI capex; blowout 2Q26 (rev +24%, cloud +82%) but FY26 capex raised to $195-205bn and quarterly FCF went negative -$5.9bn | strengthening",
    "NBIS": "Re-entered 2026-07-28 at 3sh after the 07-24 stop-out. Neocloud GPU-as-a-service; highest ATR in the book at 14.89% | watch",
    "IREN": "Re-entered 2026-07-28 at 10sh after the 07-24 stop-out. Bitcoin-mining infra pivoted to AI/GPU cloud; ATR 11.47% | watch"
